        <mxCell id="a93" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 26px;&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Agents are started with the invoice_id only. Vendor-written text reaches a model only as a tool result, and the Bedrock Guardrail scans every tool result first.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Every Lambda has its own IAM role. Only pay_invoice can write the payments ledger and PO balances.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The tools API accepts only the AgentCore Gateway role (resource policy). No route exists to create or edit vendors, POs or bank details.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The Cedar policy only permits pay_invoice at or under $2,000 (200000 cents).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- CloudFront is a global service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Payments are simulated: they are written to a DynamoDB ledger and no bank is called." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=8;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1380" y="880" width="370" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
